   "design": "Questions live in a tagged item bank from which the exam is compiled and formatted. Closed questions are marked by answer key with item statistics. Open answers are grouped by similarity so the teacher grades each group once and reads every answer; no model proposes scores. The test platform computes totals and grades from the marks. Writing questions, colleague review, invigilation, grading, registering grades and the review session stay with the teacher as appointed examiner.",
   "previous_blocker": "Exams were assembled, marked and totalled by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Item banks, closed-question marking and answer grouping.",
   "still_hard": "Open answers that need careful reading.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing what a wrong answer reveals about understanding.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less marking and totalling; grading judgement stays.",
